      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "SolarQuotes recommendations were very good, but I contracted a small company, Local Power - recommended by a friend who used them a few years ago - who use their 'smallness' to their advantage:They don't have the margins to go back and forth 'fixing' mistakes, so ensure they have everything sorted before the installation process.They took considerable time to design the 'best' system to suit my requirementsThey did a very comprehensive audit of my roof and aspect (not just using satellite photos)They have used the same team of installers (sub-contracted) for over 10 years.A week before the install, I asked for an ‘extra’:could they throw an ethernet cable (I’d already purchased) from the inverter through the roof to the ceiling above my router. I then intended to later kick a tile and get the cable down to ground level. Instead, the installers dropped the cable down so I could pull it through my wall. A small, but very welcome ‘extra’ bit of service.Local Power wasn’t the cheapest and it was a tight decision between them and one of SolarQuotes’ recommended suppliers but, when I weighed up all the positives of the quoting process, the recommended equipment, and extra advice, Local Power came out on top.The pre- and post- sales service has also been impeccable - I had a few queries on changing set-ups, and other matters. All were answered compressively and punctually.I would not hesitate to recommend Local Power (they've been around since 2007!) to be one of the companies to quote on any new solar installation.",
